 "capsule": "The Republic of the Congo (Congo-Brazzaville), which gained independence from France in August 1960, adopted single-party 'scientific socialist' rule under Alphonse Massamba-Debat's 1963 constitution and became explicitly Marxist-Leninist as the People's Republic of the Congo from 1970 to 1991. Multiparty elections in 1992 gave way to civil war later in the decade, after which Denis Sassou Nguesso, president from 1979 to 1992, returned to power in 1997 and has ruled the oil-producing state ever since.",
